From 46242bab5e571a61dbd115260920e876cb6eda02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hardening <hardening@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] build: cut the image from 6.49 GB to 2.87 GB; make bbot
 work unprivileged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five changes, all verified against a built image:

1. bbot moved into a throwaway `bbotdeps` stage. `--install-all-deps` apt-installs
   gcc/make/libssl-dev/7z/xz, pip-installs 40 module packages and runs ansible-galaxy;
   its dry-run also downloads bbot's per-module tool cache into $HOME: a second
   Chromium (693 MB), a second Node (164 MB), jadx (110 MB), trufflehog, gowitness,
   trajan, retirejs — 1.5 GB. None of it was usable: it lived in /root, which the
   runtime user (uid 10001) cannot read. Only /opt/bbot plus bbot's config is copied.

2. bbot's prepared home is seeded under /home/artex instead. Without a core-dep marker
   in ~/.bbot/cache, bbot's installer shells out to `sudo` for apt; the image has no
   sudo and bbot catches only CalledProcessError, so a scan died with
   FileNotFoundError. The build now writes the marker, bbot.yml/secrets.yml and the
   ansible collection as the runtime user's files, and the runtime hands them over.
   Verified: `bbot --dry-run -m wafw00f,sslcert,paramminer_getparams` -> 15/15 modules,
   exit 0, as uid 10001 (this was broken before the size work, not because of it).

3. Playwright installs `--only-shell`: @playwright/mcp is launched with --headless
   (db/db.go), which runs chromium-headless-shell, so the 422 MB headed Chromium was
   never started. Headless launch verified (renders a page, ffmpeg kept for video).

4. npm and pip caches are removed in the layer that creates them (55 MB + 92 MB).

5. p7zip-full/xz-utils added to the runtime apt list: bbot needs them to unpack the
   tools it now downloads on first use, and they were previously pulled in only as a
   side effect of bbot's build-time apt install.

Also adds BBOT-MODULE-DEPS.md: the 40 unhashed distributions bbot pulls on top of
requirements-bbot.lock (234 MB, newest-compatible resolution, so the set can drift
between builds), with a script to regenerate it.
